desc:Hermit [hands-free jam synth] (GFX)
//tags: instrument synth arpeggiator sequencer chords drums bass backing jam lfo phaser arcana
//author: GardenFX
// by JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Requires gfx-drift, gfx-output, gfx-ui, gfx-panel, gfx-instrument and gfx-voice (.jsfx-inc) in the same folder.
//
// THE HERMIT (card IX of the GFX Arcana series): the lantern-bearer alone on the mountain at night. A hands-free
// synth to jam with: it plays a chord sequence by itself - arpeggio or step sequence, a pad, a bass line and a drum
// loop - while eight LFOs keep everything moving. Put it on a track, press START and play, pick up the guitar.
//   CHORDS     eight slots, each a ROOT, a chord TYPE (Maj, m, 7, m7, maj7, 6, m6, sus2, sus4, 7sus4, 9, m9, add9,
//              dim, m7b5, +) and a length in BARS. The sequence plays the slots in turn and loops; a slot set to
//              0 bars ends the sequence there. TRANSPOSE moves the whole sequence.
//   PLAY       START / STOP: the master switch. FOLLOW on: it plays while REAPER plays, locked to the project's tempo
//              and bars (bar 1 = the start of the project). FOLLOW off: it runs on its own from bar 1, at the
//              project tempo, from the moment START is pressed. SWING delays the off-beat sixteenths.
//              TRANSPORT (lit by default): REAPER's play / record presses START and its stop presses STOP; the keys
//              still work by hand. Off, START / STOP ignore the transport.
//   SYNTH      ARP or SEQ (or off). ARP: UP, DOWN, UP-DOWN, RANDOM, CHORD (all at once), THUMB (the root between the
//              others); RATE 1/4 - 1/32 (with triplets), OCTAVES 1-4, GATE, REGISTER. SEQ: sixteen steps that name
//              chord tones (1-4, and 1+ to 4+ an octave up, or a rest), LENGTH 1-16 - the same figure follows every
//              chord.
//   VOICE      two oscillators whose WAVE morphs triangle > saw > square > pulse; OSC 2 DETUNE and OCTAVE, MIX, PW;
//              a 12 dB low-pass with CUTOFF, RESO and an ENVELOPE amount; LENGTH sets attack, decay, sustain and
//              release together, from short plucks to long swells; SPREAD pans the notes; ACCENT the velocity.
//   PAD        the chord held on the same voice, under the synth part: LEVEL, REGISTER, its own LENGTH, CLOSE or
//              OPEN voicing.
//   BASS       the Bass 1X engine (saw or pulse, sub, LADDER or ACID filter, accent, glide) playing a FIGURE from
//              the sequence: DRONE (the root held, gliding to the next chord), PULSE (eighth-note roots), OSTINATO
//              (a root-octave-fifth figure) or STEPS (the synth's sixteen steps, down low). CUTOFF, RESO, ENV, SUB,
//              GLIDE, OCTAVE, ON / OFF.
//   DRUMS      the Deep 16 engine as a one-bar loop: KICK, SNARE, HAT, OPEN HAT and PERC lanes of sixteen steps,
//              six STYLES to start from (MOTORIK, KRAUT, LATIN, HALF-TIME, TRIBAL, SPARSE), every step editable.
//              DECAY, ON / OFF; it swings with SWING.
//   LFO 1-8    SINE, TRIANGLE, SAW, SQUARE, S&H, SMOOTH; RATE free or synced; DEPTH (+/-); DESTINATION: PITCH,
//              TUNING (osc 2 detune), WAVE, PW, CUTOFF, RESO, LENGTH, AMP, PAN, DELAY SEND, REVERB SEND, ARP GATE,
//              PAD LEVEL, BASS CUTOFF, NEXT LFO RATE (the next LFO speeds up and slows down), OCTAVE (stepped).
//   FX         a slow PHASER (on the synth and pad), a dark tape-style ping-pong DELAY (synced) and a REVERB.
//   MIXER      LEVEL, DELAY and REVERB sends for the SYNTH, the PAD, the BASS and the DRUMS.
//   FATE (the series' drift, 0-100 %, 50 % = the standard amount): tape wow and tuning wander - the whole band
//              wobbles gently in pitch and every note lands a little differently in tune.
//   VOLUME and SAT (the output soft clip is always on).

import gfx-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-ui.jsfx-inc
import gfx-panel.jsfx-inc
import gfx-instrument.jsfx-inc
import gfx-voice.jsfx-inc

